diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 17f9658..01d9ae4 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,44 @@ proot
 [![Travis build status](https://travis-ci.org/termux/proot.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/termux/proot)
 
 This is a copy of [the PRoot project](https://github.com/proot-me/PRoot/) with patches applied to work better under [Termux](https://termux.com).
+
+Cgroup v2 emulation
+-------------------
+
+`--cgroup` presents `/sys/fs/cgroup` as a private cgroup v2 hierarchy even
+when the app UID cannot create real cgroups:
+
+```sh
+proot --cgroup -0 -r rootfs -w / /bin/sh
+```
+
+The emulation covers the non-resource parts of cgroup v2 that a service
+manager needs:
+
+* hierarchical directories (`mkdir`, `rmdir`, nested groups, rename);
+* `cgroup.procs` and `cgroup.threads` read/write, fork inheritance and
+  per-process migration (including whole-thread-group moves);
+* `cgroup.kill` (recursive), `cgroup.freeze` (real stop/resume through
+  PRoot's ptrace event loop), `cgroup.events` with inotify updates;
+* `cgroup.controllers`, `cgroup.subtree_control` delegation bookkeeping,
+  `cgroup.stat`, `cgroup.type`, `cgroup.max.depth`,
+  `cgroup.max.descendants`, `cgroup.pressure`;
+* `/proc/<pid>/cgroup`, `/proc/cgroups`, a cgroup2 `statfs` magic and a
+  synthetic mountinfo entry, including extra `mount -t cgroup2` targets.
+
+Membership is derived from unprivileged data: `/proc/<pid>/stat` (`ppid`,
+`pgrp`, session, `starttime`) plus PRoot's fork/clone/exit events.  When a
+process is reparented or calls `setsid`, its session/process-group anchor
+keeps it in the right virtual group.
+
+Resource controllers (`memory.max`, `cpu.max`, `pids.max`, I/O weights,
+...) are intentionally **not** implemented: a rootless process cannot
+enforce them, and exposing fake limits is worse than reporting them as
+unavailable.  `cgroup.controllers` reports the available controller names,
+but their resource files do not exist.
+
+Run the behaviour suite with:
+
+```sh
+bash tests/cgroup/run.sh
+```
