+/*
+ * cgroup v2 emulation for unprivileged PRoot.
+ *
+ * A container often wants a cgroup hierarchy even though the kernel (or
+ * Android) does not let its owner create one.  This extension presents
+ * /sys/fs/cgroup as a private cgroup2 hierarchy backed by a PRoot temp
+ * directory.  Membership is tracked with the same information an
+ * unprivileged process can read without cgroupfs: /proc/<pid>/stat
+ * (ppid, pgrp, session and starttime) plus the tracee events PRoot already
+ * receives for fork/clone/exit.  Every file operation that matters to a
+ * service manager is implemented:
+ *
+ *   cgroup.procs / cgroup.threads   read, migrate, inherit on fork
+ *   cgroup.kill                     kill the whole subtree
+ *   cgroup.freeze                   SIGSTOP/SIGCONT the subtree
+ *   cgroup.events                   populated/frozen, inotify-friendly
+ *   cgroup.controllers/subtree_control  delegation bookkeeping
+ *   cgroup.stat, cgroup.type, cgroup.max.*, cgroup.pressure
+ *
+ * Resource controllers are intentionally not implemented: there is no
+ * unprivileged way to enforce memory/CPU/IO limits, and pretending to
+ * enforce them is worse than reporting an empty controller set.  The
+ * hierarchy, lifecycle and delegation parts are complete.
+ */
